<title>USA: First Virginia Banks Inc Q2 shr rises.</title>
<headline>First Virginia Banks Inc Q2 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>FALLS CHURCH, Va. 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months ended  Six Months Ended</p>
<p>						 June 30	June 30</p>
<p>					1997     1996     1997     1996</p>
<p> Interest income	  $  156,341  146,379  302,902  291,684</p>
<p> Interest expense	     54,647   52,447  106,254  107,116</p>
<p> Net interest income	 101,694   93,932  196,648  184,568</p>
<p> Provision for loan losses   5,248    5,861    8,590    8,151</p>
<p> Noninterest income	   25,007   25,138   48,240   48,566</p>
<p> Noninterest expenses	 73,360   69,830  143,101  138,317</p>
<p>Provision for income taxes</p>
<p>				    16,740   14,805   32,447   29,709</p>
<p> Net income		     31,353   28,574   60,750   56,957</p>
<p> Net income per common share  0.94     0.85     1.85     1.69</p>
<p>		  (Dollars in thousands, except per-share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: As a consequence of additional shares issued for the acquisition of Premier, the oustanding shares at the end of the quarter increased 11 percent to 35.318 million shares.</p>
